WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.309
This is a stuck (impacted) lower wisdom tooth.

00:00:03.659 --> 00:00:05.451
Its roots wrap around a nerve.

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:09.023
Taking it out can damage the nerve and make your lip and chin numb.

00:00:09.823 --> 00:00:11.529
The red part is the nerve.

00:00:11.879 --> 00:00:14.781
It gives feeling to the lower teeth, gums, lip and chin.

00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:18.397
As the tooth comes out, the nerve can be pressed or cut.

00:00:19.197 --> 00:00:23.997
For a tooth like this, rates vary, but about 7 in 100 may get nerve damage.

00:00:24.347 --> 00:00:26.224
Most get better within a few months.

00:00:26.574 --> 00:00:29.926
About 1 in 100 may have damage that does not go away,

00:00:29.926 --> 00:00:31.950
and for most of them it is mild.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:36.569
So it is a good idea to see a specialist (an oral surgeon) first.
